@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il05-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il05-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-k`
IMPORT `nii-s348-maximum-minimum`
IMPORT `nii-s342-liability-and-deduction`

-- TESTS for row IL-05. Every expected value comes from the SOURCE (a cell of Schedule K or J, a limb of
-- s 342 or s 348) or from what the REGULATOR prints (the National Insurance Institute's pages, fetched
-- 2026-10-06; URLs and sha256 below and in nii-il05-published-figures.l4). Each was worked out before
-- this module was run, by a computation over the source's figures that does not use this encoding
-- (exact fractions in Python; NOTES.md section 0). A SCENARIO value (a figure for a year not yet
-- published, an update of the average wage that did not happen) is named as one.
--
-- Every assertion here is expected to be satisfied. The checks expected to FAIL, because the source
-- is inconsistent with itself, are in nii-il05-tests-expected-red.l4, with their exact count.
--
-- The Institute's printed figures this module compares with (test expectations, not law), all fetched
-- 2026-10-06 with curl, not deposited:
--   self-employed rates page (14:49:42Z, sha256 5d1e1a49…7567): maximum income 51,910 a month; "one
--     whose income is below 3,442 NIS a month pays contributions on the minimum income"; from 01.01.2026.
--   rates page for those who are neither (14:49:55Z, sha256 1c86c85f…8e92): with no income, National
--     Insurance 143 a month and health insurance 123, 266 in all; the January 2026 example, rent of
--     12,000, "income up to 3,442 a month is exempt", charged on 8,558, 931.29 + 104.05 = 1,035.
--   yeshiva student, amount page (14:51:01Z, sha256 39720f8c…125a): 171 a month at the minimum, from
--     01.01.2026 (National Insurance and health insurance together).
--   minimum and maximum income tables (self-employed 14:49:44Z, sha256 c8f8edf3…0a16; neither
--     14:53:32Z, sha256 8bc34ff3…f6be): from 01/01/2025, self-employed minimum 3,134 and maximum
--     50,695 a month; neither, 5% 627 and 15% 1,880 a month.
--   average wage page (14:49:57Z): for contributions, 2025, 12,379 (s 1) and 12,536 (s 2).

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures`

`the 2026 figures` MEANS `the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published`
`the full minimum wage in 2026` MEANS `the full monthly minimum wage in the first month of each quarter of 2026`

-- The same year with the average wage under s 1, to show what the Institute's figures do NOT match.
`the 2026 figures, with the average wage under section 1` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2026
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS `the basic amount under paragraph (3) from 1 January 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS `the average wage from 1 January 2026 under section 1, for contributions, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS EMPTY

-- 2025, from the Institute's tables: basic amount 3 from 1.01.2025 10,139; the average wage for
-- contributions under s 2 for 2025, 12,536. Used only to test the schedule's arithmetic against the
-- Institute's 2025 table; this row does not answer 2025 periods.
`the 2025 figures, from the Institute's tables` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2025
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS 10_139
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS 12_536
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS EMPTY

-- SCENARIO: a year in which the average wage is updated on 1 April, 1 July and 1 October, to tell
-- apart the months items 2, 3 and 4 read.
`a scenario year with three updates of the average wage` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2030
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS 10_000
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS 13_000
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS
            LIST (`An update of the average wage within the tax year` WITH `the month of the update` IS 4,  `the average wage as updated` IS 13_200)
               , (`An update of the average wage within the tax year` WITH `the month of the update` IS 7,  `the average wage as updated` IS 13_400)
               , (`An update of the average wage within the tax year` WITH `the month of the update` IS 10, `the average wage as updated` IS 13_600)

-- SCENARIO: figures for 2027, which were not published on 2026-10-06.
`scenario figures for 2027` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2027
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS 10_600
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS 14_000
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS EMPTY

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A period under Schedule K`
`in month` n MEANS `a month of the tax year` n

`the first quarter`  MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 January`
`the second quarter` MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 April`
`the third quarter`  MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 July`
`the fourth quarter` MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 October`
`the whole year`     MEANS `the whole tax year`

`neither` MEANS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`

§§ `Fixtures — cases for section 348`

GIVEN `the column` IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the year`   IS A NUMBER
      `the period` IS A `A period under Schedule K`
      `work`       IS A NUMBER
      `other`      IS A NUMBER
