#ASSERT ROUND (`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 4, another insured person` `, for` (`in month` 1) `, under` `the 2025 figures, from the Institute's tables` `and` NOTHING) EQUALS 1_880

§§ `Fork F1 — the average wage the Institute's figures match`

-- With the s 2 figure (13,769) the schedule gives the Institute's 2026 figures; with the s 1 figure
-- (13,566) it does not. National Insurance on the item 4 minimum at 6.92% (the rate the Institute prints
-- for one who is neither, up to the threshold): 143 a month. On the item 3 minimum, 48, which with the
-- 123 of health insurance the Institute prints for one with no income makes the 171 it prints for a
-- yeshiva student.
#ASSERT ROUND (`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 4, another insured person` `, for` (`in month` 1) `, under` `the 2026 figures` `and` NOTHING TIMES 6.92%) EQUALS 143
#ASSERT ROUND (`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` `, for` (`in month` 1) `, under` `the 2026 figures` `and` NOTHING TIMES 6.92%) PLUS 123 EQUALS 171
#ASSERT NOT (ROUND (`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 2, a self-employed person` `, for` (`in month` 1) `, under` `the 2026 figures, with the average wage under section 1` `and` NOTHING) EQUALS 3_442)
#ASSERT NOT (ROUND (`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 4, another insured person` `, for` (`in month` 1) `, under` `the 2026 figures, with the average wage under section 1` `and` NOTHING TIMES 6.92%) EQUALS 143)
#ASSERT NOT (ROUND (`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` `, for` (`in month` 1) `, under` `the 2026 figures, with the average wage under section 1` `and` NOTHING TIMES 6.92%) PLUS 123 EQUALS 171)

