§§ `Section 342(a)-(b) — who is liable`

#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH `column` IS `an employee`, `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the employer, for the employee`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH `column` IS `a self-employed person`, `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the insured person, for himself`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH `column` IS `neither`, `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the insured person, for himself`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH `column` IS `neither`, `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS TRUE) EQUALS `no one: an insured woman under Chapter C only, as the wife of an insured person, is not liable`

§§ `Fixtures — cases for section 342`

`all nine branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`
       , `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- Column D of the 2026 (temporary) version, on the part of the wage not above the threshold (source
-- lines 4720-4729): maternity 0.10, accident injury 0.03, unemployment 0.02, disability 0.29,
-- long-term care 0.03, senior citizens and survivors 0.57; "–" for the other branches. Applied to a
-- wage not above 7,703, these are the whole column D amounts.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
`the 2026 column D amounts on a wage, not above the threshold, of` x MEANS
    LIST (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `maternity`,                     `amount` IS x TIMES 0.10%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `accident injury`,               `amount` IS x TIMES 0.03%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `unemployment`,                  `amount` IS x TIMES 0.02%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `disability`,                    `amount` IS x TIMES 0.29%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `long-term care`,                `amount` IS x TIMES 0.03%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `senior citizens and survivors`, `amount` IS x TIMES 0.57%)

-- SCENARIO: column D of the permanent version (source lines 4738-4747), with the threshold at 8,000,
-- where its upper part begins (heading at source line 4736): lower 0.04, 0.01, 0.01, 0.11, 0.01, 0.22;
-- upper 0.87, 0.07, 0.21, 1.86, 0.14, 1.52.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
`the permanent version's column D amounts, with the threshold at 8,000, on a wage of` x MEANS
    LIST (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `maternity`,                     `amount` IS `the part not above 8,000` TIMES 0.04% PLUS `the part above 8,000` TIMES 0.87%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `accident injury`,               `amount` IS `the part not above 8,000` TIMES 0.01% PLUS `the part above 8,000` TIMES 0.07%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `unemployment`,                  `amount` IS `the part not above 8,000` TIMES 0.01% PLUS `the part above 8,000` TIMES 0.21%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `disability`,                    `amount` IS `the part not above 8,000` TIMES 0.11% PLUS `the part above 8,000` TIMES 1.86%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `long-term care`,                `amount` IS `the part not above 8,000` TIMES 0.01% PLUS `the part above 8,000` TIMES 0.14%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `senior citizens and survivors`, `amount` IS `the part not above 8,000` TIMES 0.22% PLUS `the part above 8,000` TIMES 1.52%)
    WHERE
        `the part not above 8,000` MEANS min x 8_000
        `the part above 8,000` MEANS max 0 (x MINUS 8_000)

GIVEN `the month`    IS A NUMBER
      `the year`     IS A NUMBER
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      `the amounts`  IS A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
      `the pension`  IS A `The senior citizen pension in the month`
      `the person`   IS A `The insured person, for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)`
      `the birthday` IS A DATE
      `police`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
`the employee's month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, paying` `the branches` `, with` `the amounts` `, the pension` `the pension` `, for` `the person` `born on` `the birthday` `, a police or prison officer` `police` MEANS
    `An employee's month under section 342(c)` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS `the year`
        `month`                                                               IS `the month`
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS `the branches`
        `the column D amounts on the wage`                                    IS `the amounts`
        `senior citizen pension`                                              IS `the pension`
        `the insured person`                                                  IS `the person`
        `date of birth`                                                       IS `the birthday`
        `a police officer or a prison officer`                                IS `police`
        `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)` IS FALSE

-- An ordinary employee: all nine branches, no pension, a man born in 1980, not a police officer.
GIVEN `the month`   IS A NUMBER
      `the year`    IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts` IS A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
GIVETH AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
`an ordinary employee's month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, with` `the amounts` MEANS
    `the employee's month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `the amounts` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE

`a wage of 7,000 in 2026` MEANS `the 2026 column D amounts on a wage, not above the threshold, of` 7_000

§§ `Section 342(c)(1) — the deduction`

-- 7,000 × 1.04% (the six cells sum to 1.04, the Institute's employee rate up to the threshold) = 72.8.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`) EQUALS 72.8
#ASSERT `s 342(c)(1) — the branches in which the employer deducts, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`) EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`
-- A non-resident employee pays maternity only (s 335(a)): 7,000 × 0.10% = 7.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` (LIST `maternity`) `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 7
-- An amount the case gives for a branch (c)(1) does not name is not deducted.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` ((`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `children`, `amount` IS 99) FOLLOWED BY `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`)) EQUALS 72.8
-- A branch (c)(1) names, with no amount given: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` (LIST (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `maternity`, `amount` IS 7))) BECAUSE "the case gives no column D amount for a branch in which the employer deducts"

§§ `Section 342(c)(2) — no deduction`

-- A police or prison officer: not item 6 (unemployment, 7,000 × 0.02% = 1.4).
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` TRUE) EQUALS 71.4
#ASSERT `s 342(c)(2) — the amount by which the employer may reduce the contributions he is liable for, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` TRUE) EQUALS 1.4
-- A senior citizen pension payable for the whole month: no deduction; the employer may reduce by 72.8.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `payable for the whole month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 342(c)(2) — the amount by which the employer may reduce the contributions he is liable for, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `payable for the whole month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 72.8
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `payable for part of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) BECAUSE "section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the senior citizen pension is payable for part of it"
-- A man born 15 March 1956 reaches 70 on 15 March 2026: February deducts, March is declined, April does not.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 2 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 3 15) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 72.8
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 3 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 3 15) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) BECAUSE "section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the insured reaches the age during it"
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 3 15) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- Born on the first of a month: the whole of that month is after the age.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 4 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 3 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 4 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 72.8
-- A woman born June 1956: Part D fixes 70 for a woman born in May 1950 or later (source line 4453), 840 months.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 6 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` (`a woman` 840) `born on` (YMD 1956 6 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 5 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` (`a woman` 840) `born on` (YMD 1956 6 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 72.8
-- SCENARIO: a woman whose Part D age is 69 and 8 months (836), born 1 July 1956, reaches it on 1 March
-- 2026, four months before a man born the same day would.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 3 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` (`a woman` 836) `born on` (YMD 1956 7 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 3 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 7 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 72.8

§§ `Section 342(c) — the years answered, and the regulations`

#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 12 `of` 2025 `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`) BECAUSE "this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 13 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`) BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`An employee's month under section 342(c)` WITH `tax year` IS 2026, `month` IS 4, `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335` IS `all nine branches`, `the column D amounts on the wage` IS `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`, `senior citizen pension` IS `not payable for any of the month`, `the insured person` IS `a man`, `date of birth` IS YMD 1980 1 1, `a police officer or a prison officer` IS FALSE, `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)` IS TRUE) BECAUSE "the deduction is governed by regulations under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4), which are not encoded here"

§§ `Section 342(d) — several employers (scenario: permanent version, threshold 8,000)`

-- Two employers each paying 6,000 deduct 24 each (6,000 × 0.40%); on the total of 12,000 as one
-- employer's wage, 8,000 × 0.40% + 4,000 × 4.67% = 218.8. The employee pays 170.8.
`the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` MEANS
    `an ordinary employee's month` 2 `of` 2027 `, with` (`the permanent version's column D amounts, with the threshold at 8,000, on a wage of` 12_000)

#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 2 `of` 2027 `, with` (`the permanent version's column D amounts, with the threshold at 8,000, on a wage of` 6_000)) EQUALS 24
-- RE-POINTED IN 0.3.0 to the items' reading by name (row IL-04's fork F4, ruled 2026-10-07: the
-- printed totals govern by default): the four assertions below that turn on column D's upper part,
-- values unchanged. At the printed totals, below ("Version 0.3.0").
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0 EQUALS 218.8
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 24, 24) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0 EQUALS `the employee pays the difference` 170.8
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 300, 100) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0 EQUALS `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference` 181.2
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 200, 18.8) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0 EQUALS `neither paragraph: the actual deduction equals the coordinated contributions`
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 24) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` EQUALS `section 342(d) does not apply: the insured person works for one employer`

§§ `Section 342(e1) — a renewed kibbutz member (same scenario)`

GIVEN `meets 3A(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `meets 3A(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deducted`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)`
`a kibbutz member: 3A(a)` `meets 3A(a)` `, 3A(b)` `meets 3A(b)` `, the other employer deducted` `deducted` MEANS
    `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)` WITH
        `meets section 3A(a)`                                                 IS `meets 3A(a)`
        `works as stated in section 3A(b)`                                    IS `meets 3A(b)`
        `the member's month, as if paid by one employer`                      IS `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer`
        `contributions deducted for the member's wage by the other employer for the month` IS `deducted`

#ASSERT `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` (`a kibbutz member: 3A(a)` TRUE `, 3A(b)` TRUE `, the other employer deducted` 24) EQUALS 194.8
#ASSERT `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` (`a kibbutz member: 3A(a)` TRUE `, 3A(b)` FALSE `, the other employer deducted` 24) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` (`a kibbutz member: 3A(a)` FALSE `, 3A(b)` TRUE `, the other employer deducted` 24) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` (`a kibbutz member: 3A(a)` TRUE `, 3A(b)` TRUE `, the other employer deducted` 300) BECAUSE "section 342(e1) does not say what follows when the other employer deducted more than the coordinated contributions"

§§ `Section 342(f) — an employee who is also self-employed`

GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `the wage`  IS A NUMBER
      `the other` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An employee who is also self-employed, in a month`
`a month of` `the year` `with a wage of` `the wage` `and self-employed income of` `the other` MEANS
    `An employee who is also self-employed, in a month` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS `the year`
        `month`                                                               IS 3
        `income from the sources in sections 2(1) and 2(8) of the Income Tax Ordinance in the month` IS `the other`
        `income from the sources in section 2(2) of the Income Tax Ordinance in the month` IS `the wage`

-- Threshold 7,703 (2026). Wage 5,000: 2,703 of the self-employed income at the reduced rate.
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2026 `with a wage of` 5_000 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) EQUALS 2_703
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(1) — the part of the self-employed income not at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2026 `with a wage of` 5_000 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) `with the threshold at` 7_703 EQUALS 3_297
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2026 `with a wage of` 5_000 `and self-employed income of` 1_000) EQUALS 1_000
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2026 `with a wage of` 7_702 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2026 `with a wage of` 7_703 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(1) — the part of the self-employed income not at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2026 `with a wage of` 9_000 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) `with the threshold at` 7_703 EQUALS 6_000
-- SCENARIO threshold 8,000 for 2027.
#ASSERT `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2027 `with a wage of` 5_000 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) `with the threshold at` 8_000 EQUALS 3_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2027 `with a wage of` 5_000 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 and later had not been published when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(f)(2) — the part of the self-employed income at the reduced rate, for` (`a month of` 2025 `with a wage of` 5_000 `and self-employed income of` 6_000) BECAUSE "this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only"

§§ `Version 0.3.0 — Schedule J's printed totals or its items (row IL-04's fork F4, ruled 2026-10-07)`

-- Column D of the 2026 version on a wage of 10,000, by the items, branch by branch (source lines
-- 4720-4729): the part not above 7,703 and the part above it, 2,297. Maternity 7.703 + 19.9839 =
-- 27.6869; accident injury 2.3109 + 1.6079 = 3.9188; unemployment 1.5406 + 4.8237 = 6.3643;
-- disability 22.3387 + 42.7242 = 65.0629; long-term care 2.3109 + 3.2158 = 5.5267; senior citizens
-- and survivors 43.9071 + 34.9144 = 78.8215; together 187.3811. At the printed totals (1.04 below,
-- 7.00 above, source line 4730) the six together are 80.1112 + 160.79 = 240.9012 (row IL-04's
-- `the column D deduction under`, at its default reading).
`a wage of 10,000 in 2026, by the items` MEANS
    LIST (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `maternity`,                     `amount` IS 27.6869)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `accident injury`,               `amount` IS 3.9188)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `unemployment`,                  `amount` IS 6.3643)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `disability`,                    `amount` IS 65.0629)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `long-term care`,                `amount` IS 5.5267)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `senior citizens and survivors`, `amount` IS 78.8215)

#ASSERT `section 342(c) — the reading of Schedule J this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` EQUALS `the printed totals govern`
-- 10,000: 187.3811 at the items (the rule's 0.1.0 name, and by name), 240.9012 at the printed totals.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 10,000 in 2026, by the items`) EQUALS 187.3811
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 10,000 in 2026, by the items`) `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 240.9012 EQUALS 187.3811
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 10,000 in 2026, by the items`) `, column D at the printed totals being` 240.9012 EQUALS 240.9012
-- A police or prison officer: item 6 (unemployment) left out, its own amount 6.3643: 234.5369 at the
-- printed totals, 181.0168 at the items.
`a police officer's month of 10,000 in 2026` MEANS
    `the employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 10,000 in 2026, by the items` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` `a police officer's month of 10,000 in 2026` `, column D at the printed totals being` 240.9012 EQUALS 234.5369
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` `a police officer's month of 10,000 in 2026` EQUALS 181.0168
-- Below the threshold the two readings agree: 7,000 x 1.04% = 72.8 either way.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 4 `of` 2026 `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026`) `, column D at the printed totals being` 72.8 EQUALS 72.8
-- s 342(d), the 2027 scenario (permanent version, threshold 8,000) at the printed totals: on the
-- total of 12,000 as one employer's wage, 8,000 x 0.40% + 4,000 x 7% = 32 + 280 = 312 (the items'
-- reading gives 218.8, above). Two employers deducting 24 each: the employee pays 264; deducting 300
-- and 100: a refund of 88; deducting 200 and 18.8: the employee pays 93.2.
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, column D at the printed totals being` 312 EQUALS 312
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 24, 24) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, column D at the printed totals being` 312 EQUALS `the employee pays the difference` 264
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 300, 100) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, column D at the printed totals being` 312 EQUALS `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference` 88
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 200, 18.8) `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month of 12,000 in 2027, as if paid by one employer` `, column D at the printed totals being` 312 EQUALS `the employee pays the difference` 93.2

§§ `Version 0.4.0 — s 342(c), (d) and (e1) on the income s 348(a) takes into account (05-RC2)`

-- Every value below was worked out before this section was first run, from Schedule J column D
-- (source lines 4720-4730 and 4738-4748) and Schedule K item 1 (source line 4758), by a script over
-- exact fractions that does not use this encoding (NOTES.md, "Version 0.4.0").
--
-- Column D of the 2026 (temporary) version on an income, branch by branch (source lines 4720-4729):
-- the part not above 7,703 at the lower cells (0.10, 0.03, 0.02, 0.29, 0.03, 0.57), the part above it
-- at the upper cells (0.87, 0.07, 0.21, 1.86, 0.14, 1.52); "–" for the other branches.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
`the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` x MEANS
    LIST (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `maternity`,                     `amount` IS `the part not above 7,703` TIMES 0.10% PLUS `the part above 7,703` TIMES 0.87%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `accident injury`,               `amount` IS `the part not above 7,703` TIMES 0.03% PLUS `the part above 7,703` TIMES 0.07%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `unemployment`,                  `amount` IS `the part not above 7,703` TIMES 0.02% PLUS `the part above 7,703` TIMES 0.21%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `disability`,                    `amount` IS `the part not above 7,703` TIMES 0.29% PLUS `the part above 7,703` TIMES 1.86%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `long-term care`,                `amount` IS `the part not above 7,703` TIMES 0.03% PLUS `the part above 7,703` TIMES 0.14%)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS `senior citizens and survivors`, `amount` IS `the part not above 7,703` TIMES 0.57% PLUS `the part above 7,703` TIMES 1.52%)
    WHERE
        `the part not above 7,703` MEANS min x 7_703
        `the part above 7,703`     MEANS max 0 (x MINUS 7_703)

-- The same at the printed totals (source line 4730), for the six deduction branches together: 1.04 on
-- the part not above 7,703, 7.00 on the part above it.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` x MEANS
    (min x 7_703) TIMES 1.04% PLUS (max 0 (x MINUS 7_703)) TIMES 7%

-- SCENARIO: the permanent version at the printed totals (source line 4748), threshold 8,000: 0.40 and 7.00.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the permanent version's column D at the printed totals, with the threshold at 8,000, on an income of` x MEANS
    (min x 8_000) TIMES 0.40% PLUS (max 0 (x MINUS 8_000)) TIMES 7%

-- Months whose own column D amounts are none: the rules below do not read them (were they read, a
-- deduction branch with no amount would be declined, fork F13).
`an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` MEANS
    `an ordinary employee's month` 2 `of` 2026 `, with` EMPTY
`a police officer's February 2026, column D not given` MEANS
    `the employee's month` 2 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` EMPTY `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1980 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` TRUE
`the same in February 2027, column D not given` MEANS
    `an ordinary employee's month` 2 `of` 2027 `, with` EMPTY

-- A wage of 60,000 in February 2026. s 348(a) takes 51,910 (10,382 x 5) into account. At the printed
-- totals, 7,703 x 1.04% + 44,207 x 7% = 80.1112 + 3,094.49 = 3,174.6012; at the items, 80.1112 +
-- 44,207 x 4.67% = 2,144.5781 (the independent tester's "capped" figure, root cause 2).
