#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, under` `the 2026 figures` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 2144.5781
-- The rules that read the month's own amounts are kept: given column D on 60,000, they deduct on it,
-- 80.1112 + 52,297 x 4.67% = 2,522.3811 at the items.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 2 `of` 2026 `, with` (`the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` 60_000)) EQUALS 2522.3811
-- At the maximum, a shekel above it, and well below it (10,000: as the rules that take amounts).
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 51_910 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 3174.6012
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 51_911 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 3174.6012
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 10_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 240.9012
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 10_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, under` `the 2026 figures` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 187.3811
-- A police or prison officer at 60,000: item 6 (unemployment) on 51,910 is 1.5406 + 92.8347 =
-- 94.3753, left out: 3,080.2259 at the printed totals, 2,050.2028 at the items.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `a police officer's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 3080.2259
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `a police officer's February 2026, column D not given` `, under` `the 2026 figures` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 2050.2028
-- A man who reached 70 on 1 January 2026: nothing is deducted, and column D is not needed.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` (`the employee's month` 2 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` EMPTY `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 1 1) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 0
-- The years. 2025: declined as every s 342(c) rule declines it. 2027 at the switch: the Schedule K
-- figures for 2027 were not published. SCENARIO 2027 with figures (basic amount 10,600, so 53,000) and
-- the permanent version (threshold 8,000): 8,000 x 0.40% + 45,000 x 7% = 32 + 3,150 = 3,182 at the
-- printed totals; 32 + 45,000 x 4.67% = 2,133.5 at the items. Figures for another year than the month's: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` (`an ordinary employee's month` 12 `of` 2025 `, with` EMPTY) `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` BECAUSE "this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `the same in February 2027, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the permanent version's column D amounts, with the threshold at 8,000, on a wage of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the permanent version's column D at the printed totals, with the threshold at 8,000, on an income of` BECAUSE "the figures Schedule K reads for 2027 and later had not been published when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `the same in February 2027, column D not given` `, under` `scenario figures for 2027` `, reading Schedule J as` `the printed totals govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the permanent version's column D amounts, with the threshold at 8,000, on a wage of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the permanent version's column D at the printed totals, with the threshold at 8,000, on an income of` EQUALS 3182
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `the same in February 2027, column D not given` `, under` `scenario figures for 2027` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the permanent version's column D amounts, with the threshold at 8,000, on a wage of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the permanent version's column D at the printed totals, with the threshold at 8,000, on an income of` EQUALS 2133.5
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` 60_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, under` `scenario figures for 2027` `, reading Schedule J as` `the printed totals govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` BECAUSE "the figures given are for another tax year than the case"
-- s 342(d): two employers each paying 40,000 in February 2026. Each deducts on its own 40,000 (below
-- the maximum): 80.1112 + 32,297 x 7% = 2,340.9012 at the printed totals, 80.1112 + 32,297 x 4.67% =
-- 1,588.3811 at the items. The coordinated contributions are on the total, 80,000, of which s 348(a)
-- takes 51,910: 3,174.6012, and the employee is refunded 4,681.8024 - 3,174.6012 = 1,507.2012 (the
-- independent tester's C2); at the items 2,144.5781, a refund of 3,176.7622 - 2,144.5781 = 1,032.1841.
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", on a total monthly income of` 80_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 3174.6012
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 2340.9012, 2340.9012) `, on a total monthly income of` 80_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference` 1507.2012
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 1588.3811, 1588.3811) `, on a total monthly income of` 80_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, under` `the 2026 figures` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference` 1032.1841
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 2340.9012) `, on a total monthly income of` 40_000 `, for` `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS `section 342(d) does not apply: the insured person works for one employer`
-- s 342(e1): a renewed kibbutz member whose total is 80,000 and whose other employer deducted
-- 2,340.9012: the kibbutz pays 3,174.6012 - 2,340.9012 = 833.7; at the items, the other employer
-- having deducted 1,588.3811, 2,144.5781 - 1,588.3811 = 556.197.
GIVEN `deducted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)`
`a kibbutz member in February 2026 whose other employer deducted` `deducted` MEANS
    `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)` WITH
        `meets section 3A(a)`                                                 IS TRUE
        `works as stated in section 3A(b)`                                    IS TRUE
        `the member's month, as if paid by one employer`                      IS `an ordinary employee's February 2026, column D not given`
        `contributions deducted for the member's wage by the other employer for the month` IS `deducted`
#ASSERT `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` (`a kibbutz member in February 2026 whose other employer deducted` 2340.9012) `, on a total monthly income of` 80_000 `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 833.7
#ASSERT `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` (`a kibbutz member in February 2026 whose other employer deducted` 1588.3811) `, on a total monthly income of` 80_000 `, under` `the 2026 figures` `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D by branch on an income being` `the 2026 column D by branch on an income of` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `the 2026 column D at the printed totals on an income of` EQUALS 556.197

§§ `Version 0.4.0 — one call for a person who is both an employee and self-employed (05-P3)`

GIVEN e IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An insured person who may be both an employee and self-employed, for section 342(a)-(b)`
`one who works as an employee` e `and as a self-employed person` s `, the wife flag` w MEANS
    `An insured person who may be both an employee and self-employed, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH
        `works as an employee`                                                          IS e
        `works as a self-employed person`                                               IS s
        `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS w

-- Both: the employer for the wage ((b)), the person for himself ((a)); each alone as the one-column rule.
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the persons liable to pay the contributions for` (`one who works as an employee` TRUE `and as a self-employed person` TRUE `, the wife flag` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the employer, for the employee`, `the insured person, for himself`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the persons liable to pay the contributions for` (`one who works as an employee` TRUE `and as a self-employed person` FALSE `, the wife flag` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the employer, for the employee`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the persons liable to pay the contributions for` (`one who works as an employee` FALSE `and as a self-employed person` TRUE `, the wife flag` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the insured person, for himself`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the persons liable to pay the contributions for` (`one who works as an employee` FALSE `and as a self-employed person` FALSE `, the wife flag` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the insured person, for himself`
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the persons liable to pay the contributions for` (`one who works as an employee` FALSE `and as a self-employed person` FALSE `, the wife flag` TRUE) EQUALS LIST `no one: an insured woman under Chapter C only, as the wife of an insured person, is not liable`

§§ `Fork DATE (BACKLOG IL-24, waits on Meng): the day an age is reached from 29 February`

-- A man born 29 February 1956 reaches 70 (840 months) on a day 2026 lacks. CURRENT BEHAVIOUR, kept
-- until IL-24 rules (fork F19, reading (i), clamp): `add months` gives 28 February 2026, so February
-- 2026 is a month in which the age is reached after its first day and is declined (fork F9), and
-- March deducts nothing. Reading (ii), roll to 1 March, would deduct 72.8 in February; reading (iii)
-- would decline February for want of a day. March is 0 under (i) and (ii).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 2 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 2 29) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) BECAUSE "section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the insured reaches the age during it"
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`the employee's month` 3 `of` 2026 `, paying` `all nine branches` `, with` `a wage of 7,000 in 2026` `, the pension` `not payable for any of the month` `, for` `a man` `born on` (YMD 1956 2 29) `, a police or prison officer` FALSE) EQUALS 0
